From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] lance-core: add a portable riscv64 SIMD-tier fallback (9.0.0)

lance-core's SIMD_SUPPORT static (src/utils/cpu.rs) picks a SIMD tier
via a `cfg`-gated closure with arms for aarch64, x86_64 and loongarch64
only; none of them match riscv64, so the closure's block has no
trailing expression there and the crate fails to compile with "expected
`SimdSupport`, found `()`". Add a `None`-tier fallback arm beside the
existing ones for every architecture without a dedicated tier.

Same change as 0002/0004-lance-{core,linalg}-riscv64-simd-fallback.patch
(which target this crate's 7.0.0 release), rebased onto the 9.0.0
crates.io release that crates/lance-context-core's `lance = "9.0.0"`
pulls in; the fallback arms themselves are unchanged. Applied (via
0003-cargo-patch-lance-crates-for-riscv64.patch) to a local copy of
lance-core 9.0.0 materialized by the workflow, since it is a transitive
crates.io dependency and cannot be patched in place (CLAUDE.md gotcha
300).

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted to lance-format/lance]

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
diff --git a/src/utils/cpu.rs b/src/utils/cpu.rs
index c4d5a97..8aefaee 100644
--- a/src/utils/cpu.rs
+++ b/src/utils/cpu.rs
@@ -210,6 +210,17 @@ pub static SIMD_SUPPORT: LazyLock<SimdSupport> = LazyLock::new(|| {
             SimdSupport::None
         }
     }
+    // riscv64 (and any other architecture without a dedicated tier above) has
+    // no SIMD kernels in lance yet; upstream's cfg arms have no catch-all, so
+    // this closure otherwise evaluates to `()` here instead of `SimdSupport`.
+    #[cfg(not(any(
+        target_arch = "aarch64",
+        target_arch = "x86_64",
+        target_arch = "loongarch64"
+    )))]
+    {
+        SimdSupport::None
+    }
 });
 
 #[cfg(target_arch = "x86_64")]
